{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations","id":1385158,"title":"Choosing the Shape of Your Destruction - Dogstar Ruminations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-01T17:57:48-07:00","id":1385158,"title":"Choosing the Shape of Your Destruction - Dogstar Ruminations","content":"Was going through usual YT video queue and watched <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-KIm0RBevNw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. Now I'm wondering how high a megatsunami you can kick off with Lore, and in general, just what sort of ceiling there is on the disasters that DR can produce. if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T18:55:48-07:00","id":1385168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As far as ceilings for DR goes, it won't destroy more than a kingdom. So like, you can't proclaim the doom of the entire Blessed Isle or the entire East or something. You could destroy Paragon or the Lap.<br /> <br /> Also it's not just natural disasters, it can uncover a dark moon night where all the dead rise to slay the living or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:00:02-07:00","id":1385286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1385168#post1385168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vA9aAwiXRYM</a><br /> <br /> As far as ceilings for DR goes, it won't destroy more than a kingdom. So like, you can't proclaim the doom of the entire Blessed Isle or the entire East or something. You could destroy Paragon or the Lap.<br /> <br /> Also it's not just natural disasters, it can uncover a dark moon night where all the dead rise to slay the living or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one sounds like it's stepping on Abyssal toes at least a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:12:40-07:00","id":1385290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1385286#post1385286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last one sounds like it's stepping on Abyssal toes at least a little.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think it's too bad. Remember, neither the Solar character who delivers the prophecy, <i>nor</i> the actual player who uses God-King's Shrike at the table, is in charge of what the actual disaster <i>is</i>. That's up to the Storyteller. In-universe, the Solar isn't creating or otherwise putting the disaster in motion, she's merely using her incredible lore and skill at forseeing the future to predict what <i>will</i> happen. It would have happened without her making her prophecy, too (and if she repudiates the prophecy, it's not her cancelling the apocalypse, it's a matter of finding some tiny error or other miscalculation, and the disaster would never actually have happened after all). <br /> <br /> So, since the disaster is under the control of the ST, if the ST feels that the most reasonably disaster for a city built on top of a giant mortuary is for the dead to rise up and devour everyone, that's fine. Solar Lore doesn't stop at the borders of Creation, or not cover creatures of darkness or death. An expert Solar prophet should be totally capable of predicting that &quot;building your city on top of a giant graveyard <i>might</i> eventually lead to a problem with the undead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:55:43-07:00","id":1385298,"title":"","content":"Reading the charm, it does seem to come from the Solar declaring what the &quot;doom&quot; will be and the universe bowing to the character's will. It's less a prophecy than a curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T14:39:25-07:00","id":1385301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1385298#post1385298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the charm, it does seem to come from the Solar declaring what the &quot;doom&quot; will be and the universe bowing to the character's will. It's less a prophecy than a curse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's (in my opinion) one of the more overwritten charms in the corebook, so it's definitely hard to tell exactly what the intent is. But I'm thinking it's meant to be a prophecy for two reasons. First, it <i>is</i> pretty clear that the Storyteller picks the nature of the doom, not the player: &quot;The Solar decides what region to research and pronounce doom upon, but the Storyteller decides the nature of the doom she divines...&quot;. Second, I feel that a prophecy fits Solar themes much better than a curse does. Solar charms are incredible uses of skill, but they are supposed to be, mostly, actual expressions of the Abilities being used. Predicting a disaster with incredible precision fits into Lore pretty neatly in that paradigm. But actually <i>causing</i> a disaster feels much more like it's changing Fate/Destiny, and <i>that</i> would be stepping on, not Abyssal, but rather <i>Sidereal</i> toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T16:27:13-07:00","id":1385318,"title":"","content":"Solar predicts that a Fae bard gets a number one hit. It's catchy, so catchy a literal ear worm grows in your head and passes from person to person until you have the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KQ6zr6kCPj8#t=1m5s\" target=\"_blank\">We Be Shufflin'</a> situation of music zombies.running a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T19:02:15-07:00","id":1385337,"title":"","content":"Looking it over the bit where it says the Solar can overturn it and the line &quot;In this case what the Solar realizes she causes to happen.&quot; Suggest there is a level of fate manipulation. Probably something like connecting dots and forcing patterns they've noticed to lead into things. Though the commitment of motes and such would probably be best explained as catalyzing it. connecting all the notes and patterns and such from their research that its pushing a minor thing into an active play position. Less causing and more solidifying a possibility into existence.<br /> <br /> As far as the extent goes, first you need five successes to get any effect from it. The description for that is a natural disaster that has relatively damming effects, so my logic is you're basically effing up an area. Might destroy or devastate towns but the big meat of it will be the ramifications of the event outside of the event.<br /> <br /> 2-4 extra successes can cause more specific and wide scale annihilation. Whereas the base one might cause major problems for Peleps because the major storms destroyed a bunch of the major docking stations making it harder for the navy to dock in for repairs, resupplies, and other important upkeep details. At this level you just wipe out the fleet. Areas and such that are problems just get destroyed, but you are still somewhat limited. It looks like if you're planning utter obliteration then you're limited to a major city, you want to reek havoc and destruction throughout a direction though you can do that its just not going to be as direct as meteors slamming into and vaporizing cities.<br /> <br /> 5+ Go nuts. You may not be able to flat out annihilate a direction, but you're basically declaring the beginning of some other campaign's third act or the showdown with a big bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T19:51:49-07:00","id":1385345,"title":"","content":"Having caused something to happen via researching isn\u2019t necessarily \u201cfate manipulation.\u201d Or, at least, no moreso than causing a kickball to get stuck in a tree by kicking it is \u201cfate manipulation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nothing in the Charm suggests the Solar\u2019s savant-like studying ability has anything to do with the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-03-2020, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T21:07:24-07:00","id":1385348,"title":"","content":"To me the most evocative part of the Charm description has always been this :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p.340</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through this Charm she reaches realization of a certain calamity that must happen, <b>and her consciousness is recognized, in turn, by the universe</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar's understanding of the world is so absolute that she knows better than the universe how reality is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> She says &quot;<i>Hey! Universe! You got that part wrong! Look at the data again, there's supposed to be a calamity about to happen here!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Universe goes &quot;<i>Whoops! You're totally right, my bad!&quot;</i> and corrects its mistake.<br /> <br /> It's basically the most Solar thing ever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:13:19-07:00","id":1386159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plastic Doll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1385298#post1385298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less a prophecy than a curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more a prophecy in the traditional sense of being the proclamation of one who speaks on behalf of a divinity. More Biblical &quot;Sodom and Gomorrah are out of luck&quot; kind of prophecy.<br /> <br /> We can quibble over the idea of whether or not the specifics can be defined by the prophet rather than by God, but it still fits into the continuity of how the Charm and ones before it works and the image it's creating.<br /> <br /> In short, it's a prophecy more because of the image of righteous authority and divine judgement spoken by a human than whether or not it's predicting the future, and that has subtle but significant connotations distinct from cursing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:17:13-07:00","id":1386162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1385301#post1385301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>that</i> would be stepping on, not Abyssal, but rather <i>Sidereal</i> toes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal toes are in causing a disaster by wrapping your fist in a burning prayer strip and punching somebody with it, and giving somebody the dubious escape clause of being able to take a really nasty degree of personal injury. There is so much in the specific details of how Sidereal personality and powers function that they can withstand the Solar milieu getting to stretch its legs into the natural space of &quot;stand at the summit of the mount and pronounce doom on the sinners below&quot;.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Abyssals can manage to have their toes stepped on a bit as well. Go ahead with your unsealing the scrolls and letting the wormwood pour from the sky. I don't believe there's any citation in scripture you can find to convince me to let the Solar Exalted go all Fabio through the medium of the shadows and apparitions of the night or bring forth lacerating chains from their anima to seal somebody into an Iron Maiden and anoint them as an unholy knight of rock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-06-2020, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:08:16-07:00","id":1386182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1386162#post1386162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidereal toes are in causing a disaster by wrapping your fist in a burning prayer strip and punching somebody with it, and giving somebody the dubious escape clause of being able to take a really nasty degree of personal injury. There is so much in the specific details of how Sidereal personality and powers function that they can withstand the Solar milieu getting to stretch its legs into the natural space of &quot;stand at the summit of the mount and pronounce doom on the sinners below&quot;.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Abyssals can manage to have their toes stepped on a bit as well. Go ahead with your unsealing the scrolls and letting the wormwood pour from the sky. I don't believe there's any citation in scripture you can find to convince me to let the Solar Exalted go all Fabio through the medium of the shadows and apparitions of the night or bring forth lacerating chains from their anima to seal somebody into an Iron Maiden and anoint them as an unholy knight of rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd probably be best to keep it to the same Ability, in which case, for Sidereals, we're comparing the prayer strip Charm that pronounces doom against an individual. For Abyssals, it's still a potential running concern, because one could reasonably expect them to stand below everything and stir dread darkness into action by pronouncing forbidden words. It seems like it would be well within the realm of emulating the Bishop or the Dowager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T20:38:09-07:00","id":1386237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1386182#post1386182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd probably be best to keep it to the same Ability, in which case, for Sidereals, we're comparing the prayer strip Charm that pronounces doom against an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it absolutely is not. Solar prognostication can be allowed to thrive and find its own character specifically <i>because</i> it only makes sense in a single Ability. In contrast to the Sidereal Exalted whose function as seers ensures that they have foresight dotted idiosyncratically through multiple ones. To deny the significance of Sidereals shaping the future with Brawl is to go beyond stepping on toes and right into shackling their legs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Abyssals, it's still a potential running concern, because one could reasonably expect them to stand below everything and stir dread darkness into action by pronouncing forbidden words. It seems like it would be well within the realm of emulating the Bishop or the Dowager.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;concern&quot; here.<br /> <br /> Still, I'll go a step further and propose that an Abyssal Lore Charm to pronounce some Biblical wrath is not merely distinguished in the aesthetic details of what it unleashes but in the necessary setup.<br /> <br /> The requirement for research means that God King's Shrike exists on that fuzzy boundary between application of a technical skill and being the representative of righteous divinity and anointed master of the universe. But those three aren't quite the motifs driving the Abyssals; the grim romance, the dance macabre, the vengeance of the downfallen world and dream of treacherously slain gods.<br /> <br /> There ought to be something different in how they set a localised end of the world in motion that makes one see all of that as vividly as one sees Lot in the Solar Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:32:52-07:00","id":1386246,"title":"","content":"One way I could see an Abyssal God King Shrike would be that the Abyssal glimpses beyond the veil and realizes exactly how the city/region will fall. She then announces it to them, very publicly. And <b>this</b> sets off a self-fulfilling prophecy, where all the horror, despair and panic that the announcement creates sends the city/region into a spiral of terrible decisions, with said terrible decisions eventually leading to the city/region's fall <b>exactly </b>as the Abyssal had announced it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:15:57-07:00","id":1386593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1386237#post1386237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it absolutely is not. Solar prognostication can be allowed to thrive and find its own character specifically <i>because</i> it only makes sense in a single Ability. In contrast to the Sidereal Exalted whose function as seers ensures that they have foresight dotted idiosyncratically through multiple ones. To deny the significance of Sidereals shaping the future with Brawl is to go beyond stepping on toes and right into shackling their legs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking single steals from an Ability or entire Ability concepts? Because the latter seem like they're so noticeable that even the causes of Misty Voyage from the original DotFA books would find it too obvious a lift, whereas that one aforementioned Sidereal capstone in DotFA Solar Sail is hiding amidst nominally Solar effects (not well, of course, but that was the problem with it and a number of other examples, sometimes even reflecting Solar Charms pilfering from already Solar-specific Adamant Sorcery).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;concern&quot; here.<br /> <br /> Still, I'll go a step further and propose that an Abyssal Lore Charm to pronounce some Biblical wrath is not merely distinguished in the aesthetic details of what it unleashes but in the necessary setup.<br /> <br /> The requirement for research means that God King's Shrike exists on that fuzzy boundary between application of a technical skill and being the representative of righteous divinity and anointed master of the universe. But those three aren't quite the motifs driving the Abyssals; the grim romance, the dance macabre, the vengeance of the downfallen world and dream of treacherously slain gods.<br /> <br /> There ought to be something different in how they set a localised end of the world in motion that makes one see all of that as vividly as one sees Lot in the Solar Charm. </div> </div> </div>Well, on the corner of things Solar Charms definitely wouldn't do, there's raising the dead, creating shadowlands, and having truck with ghosts. But we're going by Deathlord aesthetics, and one of the most likely to corner Lore as theirs is the Dowager, who seems to be the type to construct or deliberately search for dooms and then unleash them personally. So, probably like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> mentioned, but instead of relying on a breakdown of society as such, it probably involves acting like Maleficent and laying a curse on the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T21:15:01-07:00","id":1386607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385158-choosing-the-shape-of-your-destruction-dogstar-ruminations?p=1386593#post1386593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are we talking single steals from an Ability or entire Ability concepts? Because the latter seem like they're so noticeable that even the causes of Misty Voyage from the original DotFA books would find it too obvious a lift, whereas that one aforementioned Sidereal capstone in DotFA Solar Sail is hiding amidst nominally Solar effects (not well, of course, but that was the problem with it and a number of other examples, sometimes even reflecting Solar Charms pilfering from already Solar-specific Adamant Sorcery).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, what I say now I say in all sincerity, without any intention of condescension:<br /> <br /> I cannot make heads or tails of this. Can you please state it plainly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, on the corner of things Solar Charms definitely wouldn't do, there's raising the dead, creating shadowlands, and having truck with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>If raising the dead is just a showy way of bringing destruction on a location, why not?<br /> <br /> Having truck with ghosts is just talking to them, maybe backed with some Occult Charms.<br /> <br /> Right now I actually am seeing shadowlands as within the remit of their greatest power. Not fine control of them, but I see no incongruity in the authority of the Solars allowing them to punish by withholding the light. Jesus making a point by causing the fig tree to wither, writ large.<br /> <br /> I imagine Abyssals coming at these phenomena with different priorities. From them the shadowland is more than just a punishment. The Solars can lurk in darkness, but not to offer salvation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're going by Deathlord aesthetics<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I often think about how much that would be compared to the Unconquered Sun in the Solar Charms when it was first brought up, and we've got an example of what that means now. Even one of Luna in the Charms of their Chosen, come to think of it.<br /> <br /> It makes me feel as though we've got a basis for seeing these primarily in terms of Abyssal Charms, and leaning too heavily into the Deathlord references is just limiting. It's why when I described those previewed Charms I referred to invoking gothic Fabio.<br /> <br /> I hope that when Abyssals are finally published, we'll have enough to move past it.<br /> <br /> My point here is that I'd want to talk about such a Lore Charm primarily in terms of the persona and narrative it brings out in the Underworld's Lawgivers, not how it references a Deathlord. God-King's Shrike can be seen in terms of when the Unconquered Sun was more Biblical sure, but he's not the one you're playing so I want to focus on the more human image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}